# warpgate_admin_role (Resource)

Manages an admin role in Warpgate. An admin role is a named set of permissions in the admin UI and API, such as viewing and terminating sessions or editing targets. It is assigned to users with `warpgate_user_admin_role`, or through the `admin_role_mappings` of an SSO provider.

Admin roles are separate from `warpgate_role`, which grants users access to targets.

A user with any admin permission can read everything in the admin UI; the permissions control what they can change. Every permission defaults to `false`, so a role grants only what is listed.

## Example Usage

```hcl
# A security team that can watch, stop and approve sessions, but not change
# the configuration.
resource "warpgate_admin_role" "security" {
  name        = "security"
  description = "Security team"

  sessions_view      = true
  sessions_terminate = true
  approve_sessions   = true
  recordings_view    = true
  tickets_delete     = true
}

resource "warpgate_admin_role" "target_operators" {
  name = "target-operators"

  targets_create = true
  targets_edit   = true
  targets_delete = true
}
```

## Argument Reference

The following arguments are supported:

* `name` - (Required) The name of the admin role. Must be unique within the Warpgate instance.
* `description` - (Optional) A human-readable description of the admin role and its purpose.
* `targets_create` - (Optional) Allow creating targets. Default: `false`.
* `targets_edit` - (Optional) Allow editing targets. Default: `false`.
* `targets_delete` - (Optional) Allow deleting targets. Default: `false`.
* `users_create` - (Optional) Allow creating users. Default: `false`.
* `users_edit` - (Optional) Allow editing users. Default: `false`.
* `users_delete` - (Optional) Allow deleting users. Default: `false`.
* `access_roles_create` - (Optional) Allow creating access roles. Default: `false`.
* `access_roles_edit` - (Optional) Allow editing access roles. Default: `false`.
* `access_roles_delete` - (Optional) Allow deleting access roles. Default: `false`.
* `access_roles_assign` - (Optional) Allow assigning access roles to users and targets. Default: `false`.
* `sessions_view` - (Optional) Allow viewing sessions. Default: `false`.
* `sessions_terminate` - (Optional) Allow terminating sessions. Default: `false`.
* `approve_sessions` - (Optional) Allow approving sessions that wait for an administrator. Default: `false`.
* `recordings_view` - (Optional) Allow viewing session recordings. Default: `false`.
* `tickets_create` - (Optional) Allow creating tickets. Default: `false`.
* `tickets_delete` - (Optional) Allow deleting tickets. Default: `false`.
* `config_edit` - (Optional) Allow editing the global parameters. Default: `false`.
* `admin_roles_manage` - (Optional) Allow managing admin roles and their assignments. Default: `false`.
* `ticket_requests_manage` - (Optional) Allow approving and denying ticket requests. Default: `false`.

## Attribute Reference

In addition to all arguments above, the following attributes are exported:

* `id` - The ID of the admin role.

## Import

### Declarative Import Block (Terraform 1.5+ / OpenTofu 1.6+)

```hcl
import {
  to = warpgate_admin_role.security
  id = "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"
}
```

### CLI Command (Terraform / OpenTofu)

```shell
# Using Terraform CLI
terraform import warpgate_admin_role.security 12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012

# Using OpenTofu CLI
tofu import warpgate_admin_role.security 12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012
```

The built-in `warpgate:admin` role can be imported, but Warpgate refuses to delete it.

